WEBVTT

00:00.550 --> 00:02.110
In the present time,

00:02.690 --> 00:05.900
with VR headgear,
you can go into a virtual world

00:05.900 --> 00:09.030
and play as the resident of that world.

00:09.570 --> 00:13.790
VR Full-Dive games are
at the height of their popularity.

00:14.870 --> 00:17.870
And there exists

00:17.870 --> 00:22.040
a god-tier game that stands
above all other games

00:22.040 --> 00:24.630
with over thirty million
players worldwide.

00:24.630 --> 00:26.380
And the time of that game is...

00:26.380 --> 00:29.050
Shangri-La Frontier.

00:46.940 --> 00:52.870
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:08.440 --> 02:10.990
Oops, now's not the time
to marvel at this.

02:11.490 --> 02:13.240
But I can do this!

02:13.240 --> 02:15.030
I just gotta go on to the tower.

02:19.160 --> 02:20.120
What?

02:20.870 --> 02:21.580
A flame?

02:24.000 --> 02:25.500
A new move?

02:25.500 --> 02:27.290
I better be ready to use Inventoria.

02:47.880 --> 02:53.450
#49: KING OF THE DEPTHS,
PREPARE TO BE FORMALLY PULVERIZED

02:53.990 --> 02:56.710
INVENTORIA

02:56.710 --> 03:00.700
T-That was really close... I made it...

03:00.700 --> 03:02.120
What the heck was that?

03:02.120 --> 03:06.120
An ultra-speed concentrated lighting beam?

03:07.710 --> 03:11.090
The beam's shockwave alone
took away my HP.

03:11.090 --> 03:14.590
Even if I avoid a direct hit,
the range of damage is too wide.

03:15.130 --> 03:18.640
A-Anyway, I better recover my HP to full.

03:19.390 --> 03:23.350
I've got nothing to lose
even if I fail to heal in Inventoria.

03:23.350 --> 03:27.650
No wonder that dual-element orca
is called a "king."

03:28.150 --> 03:29.520
But...

03:29.520 --> 03:32.440
This is not a bad situation for a test.

03:32.440 --> 03:36.900
Judging from the angle, that attack
should hit right into the tower.

03:43.910 --> 03:45.000
All right!

03:45.750 --> 03:46.920
Time to go.

03:48.580 --> 03:52.670
If the Blocker's role is simply
to protect the tower,

03:52.670 --> 03:57.800
then I won't need to fight them
if I destroy the towers they are in.

03:59.800 --> 04:02.430
Of course, it won't be that easy.

04:04.930 --> 04:08.190
The surrounding buildings
are still as wrecked as before.

04:08.690 --> 04:12.480
That means the tower didn't get
recovered by Ctarnidd or anything.

04:13.150 --> 04:15.820
So they are indestructible objects, after all.

04:18.240 --> 04:19.240
Wha—

04:21.640 --> 04:23.160
This guy...

04:23.160 --> 04:26.370
I hid for quite a while
in Inventoria, too.

04:26.370 --> 04:28.500
Was he waiting to ambush me out here?

04:32.540 --> 04:36.820
Did they implement anti-Inventoria measures
on monsters besides Crystal Scorpions?

04:38.220 --> 04:41.760
Damn it, you devs!

04:46.770 --> 04:48.850
I seriously can't believe you!

04:50.020 --> 04:54.980
To think you'd actually pick a fight with
Atlanticus Lepnorca... The King of the Deep!

04:55.350 --> 04:57.010
Whoa, Araba?!

04:57.010 --> 05:00.320
Not even those half-rotten pseudo-fish
would try something this stupid!

05:00.320 --> 05:01.660
Y-You can fly?!

05:01.660 --> 05:03.620
I'm not flying.

05:03.620 --> 05:05.160
I'm swimming.

05:05.160 --> 05:08.170
But first, we gotta worry
about the King of the Deep.

05:08.170 --> 05:10.540
Surely now you understand
how menacing he is, right?

05:10.540 --> 05:12.210
Oh, yeah.

05:12.670 --> 05:14.380
Let's hurry up and get out of here!

05:14.380 --> 05:16.000
Fine, alright.

05:16.000 --> 05:19.420
I was just testing stuff anyway,
and I wasn't trying to kill him or anything.

05:19.420 --> 05:20.680
Hmm?

05:26.560 --> 05:30.750
Guess changing your perspective and swimming
in the air can be good every now and then.

05:30.750 --> 05:31.690
What?!

05:32.270 --> 05:36.400
I think I'm getting an idea of
how to defeat that king after all.

05:36.940 --> 05:39.570
Take down the King of the Deep, you say?!

05:39.570 --> 05:41.070
Are you sane, Sunraku?!

05:41.480 --> 05:44.110
Not in a normal way, of course.

05:44.110 --> 05:46.950
But if I can get him right
where I want him to be, then maybe.

05:54.420 --> 05:55.960
T-That was close.

05:56.470 --> 05:58.460
Araba, it's dangerous up here.

05:58.460 --> 06:00.340
Get between the buildings.

06:00.340 --> 06:02.220
I know!

06:02.970 --> 06:07.050
But Atlanticus Lepnorca
is a giant ball of belligerence

06:07.050 --> 06:09.970
who'll never give up until
he takes down his enemy!

06:10.520 --> 06:12.980
To be frank, escaping him will be difficult.

06:14.390 --> 06:16.480
Do we really have no options
but to fight him?

06:16.980 --> 06:21.990
I'm impressed you still went to save me
despite knowing all that.

06:22.360 --> 06:24.490
Either you're a pretty
nice guy or a huge idio—

06:24.490 --> 06:26.490
I owed you one!

06:26.490 --> 06:27.740
That's all.

06:28.830 --> 06:29.990
I see.

06:30.620 --> 06:33.370
But still, you can fly, huh?

06:33.370 --> 06:35.250
I didn't know that.

06:35.250 --> 06:37.750
It wasn't like I knew
how to "swim" at first.

06:37.750 --> 06:38.500
Huh?

06:38.920 --> 06:40.000
Before...

06:40.630 --> 06:43.260
How did those mermaids fly?

06:43.260 --> 06:45.760
Going by the logic you told me,
they should've fell.

06:46.230 --> 06:49.430
This is a theory, but maybe
they twisted the idea

06:49.430 --> 06:52.520
of "space with no water"
into "space with water."

06:52.520 --> 06:53.980
Hmm?

06:53.980 --> 06:57.020
In other words,
from the mermaids' perspective,

06:57.020 --> 07:01.900
it's like we were
"running inside the water."

07:02.780 --> 07:08.490
From that conversation, I figured it might
have to do with the perspective they have.

07:09.120 --> 07:10.450
Oh?

07:10.450 --> 07:13.200
So I figured,
given our familiarity with the sea,

07:13.200 --> 07:15.960
we Merman should be able to
pull the same trick.

07:16.460 --> 07:19.090
So I tried it, and here we go.

07:19.090 --> 07:22.590
A perspective you have
because you're a Merman, huh?

07:23.340 --> 07:27.090
Doesn't seem like us
players can copy that.

07:29.730 --> 07:33.350
More importantly, what do you mean
you have an idea of how to beat him?

07:34.570 --> 07:35.350
You heard me.

07:35.890 --> 07:40.230
I realized something when I saw
one of those tall towers from up high.

07:40.230 --> 07:41.980
There's something strange about it.

07:41.980 --> 07:43.480
Strange?

07:43.910 --> 07:48.160
Although taking a direct hit from
that dual-element orca's gigantic laser,

07:48.160 --> 07:51.780
the tower stood tall
like nothing happened.

07:52.500 --> 07:56.790
At first, I thought it was just
simply an indestructible object.

07:56.790 --> 08:00.540
But the surrounding rubble
and the destruction was strange.

08:02.130 --> 08:06.130
The line of rubble headed
straight for the tower

08:06.130 --> 08:09.220
was simply the laser's trail,
so that's understandable.

08:09.220 --> 08:14.970
But in addition to that, there was another
trail of rubble extending from the tower.

08:16.060 --> 08:18.310
This "turned over" city Ruluiath,

08:18.770 --> 08:21.730
as the name implies, is a city
where even concepts themselves

08:21.730 --> 08:24.570
are reversed under
the power of the "turning."

08:25.610 --> 08:30.820
If we assume that tower is still
standing thanks to Ctarnidd's ability,

08:30.820 --> 08:35.160
that tower isn't an indestructible tower,
but instead, a tower that deflects attacks.

08:35.160 --> 08:37.120
That'd make more sense.

08:37.580 --> 08:40.290
Besides, didn't you see that as well?

08:40.290 --> 08:43.380
The moment the laser
got deflected by the tower.

08:47.090 --> 08:48.260
Indeed.

08:48.260 --> 08:51.390
Now that you mention it,
it did look like that.

08:51.390 --> 08:54.890
Wait! Are you saying you're
going to use that deflection to...

08:54.890 --> 08:56.430
You got it!

08:56.430 --> 08:59.770
This time I'll take on the laser
fired directly at the tower,

09:00.270 --> 09:04.270
and have it bounced back to gauge its way
through the King of the Deep himself.

09:04.680 --> 09:05.880
That's reckless!

09:05.880 --> 09:08.780
Do you seriously think
you can pull something that precise

09:08.780 --> 09:10.530
against a raging King of the Deep?!

09:10.530 --> 09:12.700
I have a plan, of course.

09:12.700 --> 09:15.030
But I can't do it by myself.

09:15.830 --> 09:19.040
So Araba, I have a favor to ask of you.

09:21.210 --> 09:23.790
I want you to grab its attention
for one minute.

09:23.790 --> 09:24.820
What?!

09:27.800 --> 09:30.300
W-What kinda plan is that?!

09:30.730 --> 09:33.300
It hinges way too much on me!

09:33.700 --> 09:34.550
Yeah.

09:34.550 --> 09:37.560
If I fail, your life
could be in danger too!

09:37.560 --> 09:39.560
I'm aware of that!

09:39.560 --> 09:42.230
But a proud Merman can do it, right?

09:42.230 --> 09:44.560
I need you to do it
to get the position right.

09:45.980 --> 09:49.820
Looks like my luck ran out
the moment I met you back then.

09:49.820 --> 09:51.320
Don't say that.

09:51.650 --> 09:56.230
If this works out, we can take down
the King of the Deep just the two of us.

09:56.230 --> 09:58.410
Don't you want the right
to brag about that?

09:58.410 --> 10:02.330
Not even in folklore have I heard
anyone try something so foolish!

10:04.250 --> 10:06.590
Fine. I'm in.

10:07.010 --> 10:08.710
Whatever happens, happens!

10:08.710 --> 10:10.260
Let's do this, Sunraku!

10:10.260 --> 10:12.340
Okay! I'm ready whenever you are!

10:15.930 --> 10:17.220
Activate skill!

10:17.220 --> 10:18.220
GRAVITY ZERO

10:18.220 --> 10:19.220
SHANA-OH POSSESSION

10:19.220 --> 10:20.220
FLEET FLOAT

10:20.220 --> 10:22.480
Let's do this, dual-element orca.

10:22.480 --> 10:24.980
Or should I say, King of the Deep...

10:24.980 --> 10:27.690
Atlanticus Lepnorca!

10:29.320 --> 10:31.570
Time to kill the king!

10:32.440 --> 10:35.030
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

10:36.030 --> 10:38.660
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

10:47.080 --> 10:49.840
You ignored Araba and chased
after me, just as expected!

10:49.840 --> 10:52.840
You're going to keep marauding
until eat me, aren't you?

10:53.760 --> 10:57.890
First, I need to temporarily
get him off my tail.

10:57.890 --> 10:59.710
And the problem with that...

11:01.060 --> 11:04.940
...is that ambush he does
when I return from Inventoria.

11:09.000 --> 11:13.320
This guy's AI has likely
been updated by the devs

11:13.320 --> 11:17.820
to counter Inventoria
like Crystal Scorpion's.

11:17.820 --> 11:18.820
Which means...

11:21.080 --> 11:22.080
THE PREY IT WAS CHASING
SUDDENLY VANISHES

11:22.080 --> 11:22.830
IT'S GONE?!

11:23.330 --> 11:24.160
SEARCHING THE AREA

11:24.160 --> 11:25.080
FOR A WHILE FOR THE LOST PREY
Which means...

11:25.080 --> 11:26.830
IT SHOULD BE SOMEWHERE AROUND HERE!
AI that keeps watch over the place

11:26.830 --> 11:27.540
I'LL LIE IN WAIT UNTIL IT COMES BACK!
it's lost sight of!

11:27.540 --> 11:29.000
I'LL LIE IN WAIT UNTIL IT COMES BACK!

11:29.000 --> 11:31.880
I'LL LIE IN WAIT UNTIL IT COMES BACK!
So what should I do to deal with this?

11:31.880 --> 11:32.340
I'LL LIE IN WAIT UNTIL IT COMES BACK!

11:33.130 --> 11:35.090
This is my answer!

11:35.630 --> 11:38.550
Vorpal Secret Arts: Mirror of Fading!

11:43.140 --> 11:46.600
If he'll wait for me in ambush
when I instantly vanish,

11:47.060 --> 11:50.600
I'll leave a target for him to focus on
and make him think it's me.

11:51.440 --> 11:55.820
Meanwhile, I'll get outside
his view and activate Inventoria.

11:55.820 --> 11:59.620
With I'm gone,
what action his AI will take?

12:00.370 --> 12:02.660
All right, devs.

12:02.660 --> 12:06.260
Your improved AI
against me and Araba.

12:06.260 --> 12:09.450
Let's compete to see who'll win.

12:10.000 --> 12:11.380
Enter Travel!

12:13.340 --> 12:16.550
It'll be impossible to target
that beam toward the tower

12:16.550 --> 12:19.640
without dealing with that
dual-element bastard's ambush.

12:20.300 --> 12:22.510
I've got to rely on you for this.

12:23.100 --> 12:24.730
I'm counting on you, Araba!

12:25.640 --> 12:30.150
I can't believe I'm picking a fight
against that King of the Deep.

12:30.150 --> 12:33.190
You owe me a big time
for this, Sunraku!

12:34.650 --> 12:37.150
What's the matter, King of the Deep?!

12:37.150 --> 12:42.160
The proud Merman warrior Araba
is here right in front of you!

12:48.160 --> 12:50.290
Tch, he's not falling for it.

12:50.290 --> 12:53.500
He pays no heed to anybody else
until he finishes off his prey.

12:53.500 --> 12:54.670
I gotta hurry!

12:55.170 --> 12:57.550
Or else Sunraku's plan will go to waste!

12:57.550 --> 12:59.930
Steel yourself, Araba!

13:00.410 --> 13:03.850
Make him turn your way
even if it means biting his tail!

13:03.850 --> 13:09.270
Mirror of Fading is a skill that lets me "leave"
an enemy's attention towards me in place.

13:15.820 --> 13:20.360
Because I'm no longer anywhere
near when the target is gone,

13:20.360 --> 13:22.320
the moment the enemy lost me,

13:22.320 --> 13:26.700
they'd spot another target on the same
party as me right in front of them.

13:27.830 --> 13:31.580
In this situation,
what action will his AI take?

13:31.580 --> 13:35.630
According to my theory,
his ambush action will be canceled,

13:35.630 --> 13:38.590
and he'll chase after
his new target, Araba!

13:38.590 --> 13:40.300
Exit Travel!

13:44.470 --> 13:47.220
Why is suddenly charging at me?!

13:52.140 --> 13:54.650
All right, we did it, Araba!
It worked!

13:54.650 --> 13:57.230
Now just keep running away from him!

13:57.610 --> 14:00.900
Did you see that, devs?
We are the winner here!

14:01.370 --> 14:05.490
Go ahead and patch that up
after we beat Ctarnidd, okay?

14:05.490 --> 14:07.330
I have one minute.

14:07.330 --> 14:11.370
Before Araba gets eaten, I'll climb up
the tower and get in position!

14:13.500 --> 14:15.880
My goal is the midpoint of the tower.

14:16.420 --> 14:17.880
Shana-oh Possession!

14:18.420 --> 14:19.880
Gravity Zero!

14:24.050 --> 14:26.180
Is that the Blocker?

14:26.890 --> 14:30.140
It'd be nice if she could die
from the laser too.

14:30.930 --> 14:33.770
But right now, I gotta focus
on the dual-element orca!

14:35.100 --> 14:37.400
Sit tight over there for me, okay?

14:40.280 --> 14:41.400
All right.

14:42.070 --> 14:43.880
This should be around the right height.

14:45.780 --> 14:48.160
The tower that reflects attacks.

14:48.160 --> 14:51.160
It's pretty huge up close.

14:51.870 --> 14:54.040
All left is to adjust the angle.

14:55.710 --> 14:57.380
Around here?

14:57.380 --> 14:59.920
No, a little over here.

14:59.920 --> 15:01.170
All right.

15:03.130 --> 15:05.550
Araba! Over there!

15:07.220 --> 15:10.810
Dive down from there
and come to me now!

15:11.470 --> 15:12.740
Sunraku!

15:22.360 --> 15:24.700
It's heading for Sunraku again!

15:28.570 --> 15:31.740
Look at you, out for blood
just from seeing my face again.

15:31.740 --> 15:34.830
Getting all teary-eyed from the reunion?

15:35.290 --> 15:39.460
At close range,
you bite and attack with your fins.

15:39.460 --> 15:41.340
Farther away, you break out electricity.

15:41.880 --> 15:44.920
And when I'm out of
the range of your electricity,

15:44.920 --> 15:47.340
you only have one option, right?

15:49.760 --> 15:51.760
It's an old-west shootout.

15:51.760 --> 15:54.350
Or more like catching a sword
with two hands?

15:55.100 --> 15:57.940
If I wimp up and activate
Inventoria too fast,

15:57.940 --> 16:02.110
you'd shoot me down when I come back,
ruining my whole plan.

16:02.730 --> 16:04.900
But if I'm even a moment too late,

16:04.900 --> 16:08.030
with my HP, the shockwave
alone would kill me.

16:08.030 --> 16:11.620
Unlike the first time, since I'm not running,
our distance is not that far.

16:11.620 --> 16:13.870
I'll be too slow if I try to eyeball this.

16:13.870 --> 16:18.370
I won't make it unless I activate
Inventory at the moment of fire.

16:19.460 --> 16:23.130
Now, come at me, Atlanticus Lepnorca!

16:23.550 --> 16:29.130
I'll take that hyper-powered laser you're
so proud of and send it right back to you!

16:50.570 --> 16:52.410
Come on, bounce it back!

16:53.370 --> 16:54.910
Go!

16:54.910 --> 16:57.830
Hit it!

17:07.050 --> 17:09.320
Whoa!

17:10.300 --> 17:11.640
Bullseye!

17:11.640 --> 17:12.930
A direct hit!

17:29.280 --> 17:31.950
All right! That worked!

17:32.530 --> 17:35.580
But man, that was tense.

17:35.580 --> 17:39.710
The timing at the end
was nearly all instinct.

17:39.710 --> 17:42.600
You did it, Sunraku!

17:42.600 --> 17:44.210
You took down the King of the Deep!

17:44.210 --> 17:46.000
Don't be silly, Araba!

17:46.000 --> 17:48.010
It's not over yet!

17:48.390 --> 17:49.760
His flame is almost out.

17:49.760 --> 17:52.130
Now is our opportunity to
land close-range attacks!

17:52.520 --> 17:54.140
O-Oh, right!

17:54.140 --> 17:56.640
Let's rush at it in one go!

17:58.660 --> 18:00.140
That's a king for ya!

18:00.140 --> 18:03.650
You can still move even after
getting hit by that super-powerful laser?

18:04.020 --> 18:06.860
But now it's my turn!

18:06.860 --> 18:08.150
DUCUSRAM
EQUIPPED

18:11.650 --> 18:13.320
That's tough!

18:13.320 --> 18:16.490
I suppose slash attacks won't
mean much against this body.

18:16.990 --> 18:17.990
Then...

18:20.580 --> 18:22.500
GILTA BRILLE
EQUIPPED

18:22.500 --> 18:24.710
How about this?!

18:25.290 --> 18:29.130
Shake that brain! Give him a concussion!

18:31.470 --> 18:34.720
Hammer it down with
everything you got!

18:35.890 --> 18:39.970
Right! Like how you work out
all that grudges on Failia!

18:39.970 --> 18:44.230
Turn all your hatred against
that woman into power!

18:44.640 --> 18:47.690
Just thinking about her
pisses me off even more!

18:47.690 --> 18:52.280
Why do I have to go on an errand to the corner
of the map just to fix your goddamn mood?!

18:52.660 --> 18:55.490
You'll feel better after eating
a high-grade deluxe parfait?!

18:55.490 --> 18:56.950
Go eat some weed, you wench!

18:56.950 --> 19:00.620
What do you mean you'll forgive me
if I make you laugh by dancing naked?!

19:00.620 --> 19:02.330
I don't give a crap about what you think!

19:02.330 --> 19:05.290
How dare you stop me from doing
anything by locking me up in a prison

19:05.290 --> 19:08.250
for one week in reality for
"peeking at you while you're changing"!

19:08.250 --> 19:09.800
I didn't even goddamn do it!

19:09.800 --> 19:13.710
What do you mean "I don't mind
kissing you"?! Like hell I'd do that!

19:13.710 --> 19:16.090
I much rather kiss a frog!

19:16.090 --> 19:19.430
And when I reluctantly
try to do the damn thing,

19:19.430 --> 19:22.930
"Aww, not yet baby boy.
Save it for later, okay?"

19:22.930 --> 19:26.810
"It's still one hundred
years too early," you say?!

19:26.810 --> 19:29.860
Make up your freaking mind!

19:30.480 --> 19:33.650
W-What a fierce wrath...

19:34.900 --> 19:37.240
Is this the Birdian's "Desperado"

19:37.240 --> 19:37.910
I've heard about in stories?!

19:37.910 --> 19:39.620
BIRDIAN'S DESPERADO
I've heard about in stories?!

19:39.620 --> 19:40.910
BIRDIAN'S DESPERADO

19:40.910 --> 19:42.540
I should play my part too...

19:48.500 --> 19:51.800
Even the little remaining flame
he has left takes the little HP I have.

19:51.800 --> 19:55.340
If I let this guy get back up,
I'll lose my chance to attack him!

19:55.340 --> 19:57.390
I can't keep doing this forever.

19:59.470 --> 20:01.390
I'll settle it with this!

20:01.850 --> 20:04.930
Skill, Airgetlám!

20:09.190 --> 20:10.190
What?!

20:16.820 --> 20:19.990
I know saying this against
a monster is pointless, but...

20:19.990 --> 20:23.620
Rest in peace, Atlanticus Lepnorca.

20:24.830 --> 20:28.080
We've finally done it, Sunraku!

20:29.830 --> 20:31.590
No, this is...

20:31.590 --> 20:34.090
This is bad! Firing-up!

20:54.400 --> 20:57.530
Th-That was close...

20:57.530 --> 21:01.070
That bastard gave us
one hell of a parting gift...

21:03.040 --> 21:06.580
T-Truly, a King of the Deep he was.

21:06.580 --> 21:08.620
We couldn't let our
guard down until the end.

21:09.370 --> 21:12.130
He was a formidable foe,
no doubt about that.

21:13.710 --> 21:16.050
But the winner is us.

21:19.550 --> 21:23.770
The King of the Deep,
Atlanticus Lepnorca.

21:25.010 --> 21:26.930
We beat him.

21:26.930 --> 21:28.060
Yeah.

21:28.060 --> 21:32.650
Yeah! Now, what loot
do we get from him?!

21:32.650 --> 21:37.530
I can't believe we actually beat him.
Just two of us.

21:39.740 --> 21:43.280
Sunraku, huh?
What an interesting man.

21:44.160 --> 21:46.870
Aaah, I can't be happier.

21:46.870 --> 21:49.910
I feel like I can sleep
like a log tonight.

21:51.290 --> 21:53.290
Hmm? Sleep?

21:55.130 --> 21:56.420
What time is it now?

22:09.720 --> 22:12.060
5 DAYS TO X DAY
